**Amendment (Property replay evidence)** · `amend:harness:property-replay` {% set properties = rows('org.peer-network.harness.properties') %}The {{ properties | length | number }} existing properties retain their generators, shrinkers, predicates and 256-case default strength under (`conv:xchg:metatheorems-as-tests`). The fast seed policy is source-v1: SHA-256 of the UTF-8 string pn-property-seed-v1: followed by the checked source identity, taking the first eight bytes as an unsigned big-endian integer, rendered in decimal, with the cc algorithm. The same source replays the same search, while changes explore another seed; each joined result carries seed, configured successful-case count, generator and shrinker editions, scheduling/fault choices and the committed regression corpus path. Passing results account for the configured generated cases; persisted regression cases run additionally. Failed searches retain their failure and report the completed generated count as unknown rather than inventing it. All inherited PROPTEST variables are removed before the declared configuration is applied, and failure persistence remains enabled. The committed proptest-regressions files are replay inputs; newly minimized failures require review before entering that corpus. A missing seed is structural. No additional property was added to documents or cli-common merely to duplicate existing predicates.

**Definition (Replay invocation)** · `def:harness:property-replay-command` Use the decimal seed from the failed joined result; for an example result whose seed is 20261023, replay the named property with `env PROPTEST_RNG_SEED=20261023 PROPTEST_RNG_ALGORITHM=cc PROPTEST_CASES=256 PROPTEST_FORK=false PROPTEST_TIMEOUT=0 PROPTEST_MAX_SHRINK_TIME=0 PROPTEST_MAX_SHRINK_ITERS=4294967295 cargo test -p pn-interchange --locked --offline --profile gate --test properties unique_names_decoding_inverts_encoding -- --exact --nocapture`, with other PROPTEST variables unset. The two in-crate properties use `--lib` and their full cddl::tests function names instead of `--test properties`. Keep the same source, lockfile and committed regression corpus: a seed across changed generators or dependencies is not the same replay. The property result declares a configured case count, not an invented count of attempts, rejected inputs, shrink steps or persisted witnesses.

